{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112103,"nonce":"IUY3zjp0Z5nhcbGDQFWwcauYiUQ=","title":"5.2 Factions/Guests first suites (M3)","message":"Wave 5 — payoff. Depends: 5.1, 3.1 (incident forcing), 2.x serializers;\nFactions/Guests on bench (v1 modlist). MILESTONE M3 when green.\n\n## Goal\nFirst real mod suites: encode the Factions/Guests behaviors currently sitting\nin \"awaiting in-game verification\" as rwtest scenarios — starting with the\nrecurring-regulars feature.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- Factions git-bug 6072bac + Guests git-bug c6b935d (recurring regulars:\n  reunion groups, bond-weighted returners, travel cooldowns, returner stay\n  bonus) and the feature's commits/source in both repos\n- memory: recurring-regulars-feature; `_mp/actions.json` Factions+Guests\n  entries (gizmo surface = future coverage)\n- 3.1 (dev:incident) + whatever debug hooks Factions/Guests already ship —\n  AUDIT them first; if forcing a visit/return isn't cleanly possible, file\n  the needed test hook as an issue in the mod's own repo (git-bug, mod:\u003cname\u003e)\n  and implement there, not here\n\n## Scope\n- Scenario pack `tests/factions-guests/` in rwtest form:\n  1. visitor group arrives (forced) → letter observed, guests behave\n     (Hospitality integration alive), zero red errors — the smoke test\n  2. returner selection: seeded prior-visit state → forced next visit →\n     assert returner present per bond-weighting within window\n  3. travel cooldown: immediate re-visit forcing → assert cooldown respected\n     (no returner before min ticks)\n  4. returner stay bonus: compare stay duration returner vs first-timer\n     within tolerance window\n  5. mutation check: seed a deliberate regression locally (uncommitted) and\n     confirm exactly the right scenario fails, then revert\n- Each scenario documents WHICH mod behavior it pins and links the mod's\n  git-bug id.\n\n## Invariants\nProperty/window assertions only; fixtures via gen-scripts (dev-journaled);\nany mod-side test hook lands in the mod's repo with its own issue + review.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nHow prior-visit state is seeded (save fixture vs mod hook vs long natural\nrun); tolerance windows per assertion; what of slice-4d population-\nconservation invariants is cheap to assert globally (nice-to-have: a standing\n\"no pawn duplication/leak\" check).\n\n## Acceptance\n- ≥3 meaningful scenarios green on the bench, including the smoke test.\n- The mutation check demonstrably catches its seeded regression.\n- Any punted behaviors filed as follow-up issues (here or in mod repos) —\n  nothing silently dropped.\n- M3: Dorian reviews the suite output and signs off (hard gate).","files":null}]}